          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: der Zusammenhang",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "der Zusammenhang — \"the connection, the context\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Es gibt einen Zusammenhang zwischen Schlaf und Gesundheit. There is a connection between sleep and health."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: die Zusammenhänge. In diesem Zusammenhang — in this context."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Zusammenhang is built from zusammen \"together\" and the family of hängen \"to hang\", from Old High German hengen and Proto-Germanic hangijaną (EtymDB): things that hang together."
            }
          ]
        },
